# Publishing a release

Every app release must be published to **both** feeds. Do not treat one as optional.

- Public product / auto-update: https://github.com/salesforce/zana/releases
- Mirror feed: https://github.com/grebmann1/zcc-releases/releases

`electron-builder` (`npm run release:mac`, `publish.owner`/`repo` in `apps/desktop/electron-builder.yml`) only writes **salesforce/zana**. After that succeeds, create or update the matching release on **grebmann1/zcc-releases** with the same tag, body, and artifacts (`*.dmg`, `*.zip`, `*.blockmap`, `latest-mac.yml`).

## Release name is `x.y.z` only

The GitHub **release name** (title) is the semver triple from `package.json`, nothing else.

```text
✅ 2.0.3
❌ Zana Command Center 2.0.3
❌ Zana Command Center v2.0.3
❌ v2.0.3
❌ 2.0.3-arm64
```

The git **tag** stays `vx.y.z` (example: `v2.0.3`). Do not put product copy, architecture, or a leading `v` in the release name.

When using `gh release create` / `gh release edit`, pass `--title "x.y.z"` (or equivalent) on **both** repos. If a draft or published release already has a prose title, rename it to `x.y.z` before calling the release done.
